# Line endings
#
# Postkeep is developed on Windows and Linux at the same time. Without this
# file, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf) would check text files out with CRLF
# line endings and Linux with LF, which leads to diffs that change every line.
#
# Rule: all text files use LF (Unix line endings) in the repository *and* in
# the working copy, on every operating system. Current editors (VS Code,
# Notepad++, ...) handle LF without problems.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that are binary and must never be converted
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
